// Hello-world simulation driver for a real minion module: the VPU tensor-A
// register file (clocked; wraps a preview/commit RF). This is the asserted
// sim smoke of the minion side of the suite; the whole-subsystem driver
// (vpu_top_tb.prp) is tracked separately as informational.
//
// vpu_tensora_rf sits in the minion_top cone, so BOTH sim modes reach it —
// the Pyrope tree directly, and the slang re-emission of minion/verilog.
//
// The write path is preview-gated: wr_en_early_i opens the preview latch that
// captures wr_data_i, and wr_en_i commits it into the array. Holding all three
// steady drives entry 0 to the written value, which the async read port
// returns.
//
// STATUS: the minion sim scenarios PASS — this is a real elaborate + cgen +
// host-compile + run smoke, and the RF reads back 0x1234. It is both ASSERTED
// in-testbench and gated by bench/sim.sh on the "hello world" line plus the
// printed value (CORE_SIM_EXPECT data=4660). Minion is pervasively latch-based
// (preview/commit RFs) and NO module in the vpu_top cone has a latch-free
// sub-cone, so this module is also the only shape available — do not "fix"
// this file by picking another module or by loosening the gate.
//
// (Two historical notes, both now fixed upstream. First, a silent miscompile:
// the latch -> negedge-flop enable got an /*UNRESOLVED-CYCLE*/ constant-false
// commit guard and the RF read back 0; fixed in cgen_sim.cpp, regression is
// livehd's inou/prp/tests/sim/latch_sim_negedge_enable.prp. Second, the assert
// below could not be written at all — it folded to a comptime-false failure
// before cgen was reached. That was fixme.md issue 2, and the cause was NOT
// latch/negedge modelling as long assumed: `tick_statement` had no LNAST
// lowering, so the whole tick body was silently dropped and `got` kept the
// comptime value of its `mut got = 0` initializer. Fixed by lowering
// tick/step into LNAST and walking a tick body as an uncertain scope; spec
// gates are livehd's inou/prp/tests/sim/tick_comptime_{survives,opaque}.prp.)
//
// Usage: copy next to a Pyrope tree of the design (minion/pyrope, or a slang
// re-emission of minion/verilog), then:  lhd sim <dir>/tensora_rf_tb.prp
const rf = import("vpu_tensora_rf.vpu_tensora_rf")

test rf.hello(cycles:u20 = 1000) {
  mut acc = rf
  mut got = 0
  tick cycles clocks=(clock=1) {
    acc.wr_data_i = 0x1234
    acc.wr_en_early_i = 1
    acc.wr_en_i = 1
    acc.wr_addr_i = 0
    acc.rd_addr_i = 0
    step
    got = acc.rd_data_o
  }
  puts("hello world: minion vpu_tensora_rf ran {cycles} cycles, data={got}")
  assert(got == 0x1234, "vpu_tensora_rf read-back")
}
